m L158: \nL159: opened cite73†on May 16, 2026 L160: \nL161: Issue body actions\nL162: \nL163: ### What version of Kimi Code CLI is running?\nL164: \nL165: kimi, version 1.44.0\nL166: \nL167: ### Which open platform/subscription were you using?\nL168: \nL169: kimi code\nL170: ### Which model were you using?\nL171: \nL172: kimi for coding\nL173: \nL174: ### What platform is your computer?\nL175: \nL176: macos 26.5 (Darwin 25.5.0 arm64 arm)\nL177: \nL178: ### What issue are you seeing?\nL179: \nL180: In the Web UI sidebar, clicking on an archived session does not open it. The session appears in the \"Archived\" collapsible section, but clicking it has no effect — the chat area remains unchanged and the session is not loaded.\nL181: \nL182: ## Expected behavior\nL183: \nL184: The archived session should open in the main chat area, loading its conversation history.\nL185: ## Actual behavior\nL186: \nL187: Nothing happens. The session is not selected and the chat area does not update.\nL188: ## Root cause (from code inspection)\nL189: The bug is in `web/src/App.tsx`. The `useEffect` that validates `selectedSessionId` only checks the `sessions` array (active/non-archived sessions):\nL190: \nL191:     const sessionExists = sessions.some(\nL192:       (s) => s.sessionId === selectedSessionId,\nL193:     );\nL194:     if (!sessionExists) {\nL195:       selectSession(\"\"); // clears selection\nL196:     }\nL197: \nL198: \nL199:     Because archived sessions are stored separately in archivedSessions, this check incorrectly clears the selection immediately after the user clicks an archived session.\nL200: \nL201:     Additionally, currentSession only searches in sessions:\nL202: \nL203: \nL204: \nL205:     const currentSession = useMemo(\nL206:       () => sessions.find((session) => session.sessionId === selectedSessionId),\nL207:       [sessions, selectedSessionId],\nL208:     );\nL209:     Suggested fix\nL210:     Update sessionExists to also check archivedSessions:\nL211: \nL212: \nL213:     const sessionExists =\nL214:       sessions.some((s) => s.sessionId === selectedSessionId) ||\nL215:       archivedSessions.some((s) => s.sessionId === selectedSessionId);\nL216:     Update currentSession to search both arrays:\nL217: \nL218: \nL219:     const currentSession = useMemo(\nL220:       () =>\nL221:         sessions.find((session) => session.sessionId === selectedSessionId) ||\nL222:         archivedSessions.find((session) => session.sessionId === selectedSessionId),\nL223:       [sessions, archivedSessions, selectedSessionId],\nL224:     );\nL225: \nL226: \nL227:     3. Add `archivedSessions` to the `useEffect` dependency array.\nL228: \nL229:     ### What steps can reproduce the bug?\nL230: \nL231:     ## Steps to reproduce\nL232:     1. Start Kimi Web UI (`kimi web` or `/web` in CLI).\nL233:     2. Have at least one archived session (or archive an existing one via right-click → Archive).\nL234:     3. Expand the \"Archived\" section in the left sidebar.\nL235:     4. Click on any archived session.\nL236: \nL237:     ### What is the expected behavior?\nL238: \nL239:     _No response_\nL240: \nL241:     ### Additional information\nL242: \nL243:     _No response_\nL244: Reactions are currently unavailable\nL245: ## Activity\nL246: \nL247: to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? cite74†Sign in to comment L248: \nL249: ## Metadata\nL250: \nL251: ## Metadata\nL252: \nL253: ### Assignees\nL254: \nL255: No one assigned\nL256: \nL257: ### Labels\nL258: \nL259: cite71†bugSomething isn't working Something isn't working\nL260: \nL261: ### Type\nL262: \nL263: No type\nL264: \nL265: ### Projects\nL266: \nL267: No projects\nL268: \nL269: ### Milestone\nL270: \nL271: No milestone\nL272: \nL273: ### Relationships\nL274: \nL275: None yet\nL276: \nL277: ### Development\nL278: \nL279: No branches or pull requests\nL280: \nL281: ## Issue actions\nL282: \nL283:   * cite75†Image†github.githubassets.com Open in GitHub Copi